cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these interval certificates, please cite this software release and the associated paper."
title: "JNR Higgs-zero interval certificates"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Terning"
    given-names: "John"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jterning/jnr-higgs-zero-certificates"
url: "https://github.com/jterning/jnr-higgs-zero-certificates"
abstract: >-
  Rigorous multivariate Bernstein interval certificates for effective
  near-aligned charge bounds in the charge-two JNR dyonic-instanton
  Higgs-zero problem. The archived release certifies the delta=0.02 and
  delta=0.05 cases used in the associated paper.
keywords:
  - dyonic instanton
  - JNR
  - Bernstein polynomial
  - interval certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
